WEBVTT

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.270
Pardon me!

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:10.280
Is anyone home?

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:14.740
B-Bones?

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.780
Who is it?

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:21.750
It's Konju. Where are you?

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.290
Come downstairs!

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.010
Oh, Konju.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.510
You actually came over.

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:36.720
It's nice to see you, too.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:38.680
Where's Hakumei?

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:41.060
At work. She's out.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:45.940
Here's my belated housewarming gift. It's herbal tea.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.360
How very kind of you.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:54.610
It's a beautiful house, I must say.
Look at all this space.

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:56.070
Isn't it?

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.740
I'm not fond of the bones by the front door, though.

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:03.870
So? What's with the messy display in the middle?

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:05.210
I'm working!

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:13.090
I make preserved foods and some everyday necessities to sell wholesale.

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:15.840
They're sold at a place at the bottom of Potato Valley.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.760
Huh? Wait, do you mean the Mujina store?

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:20.510
Oh, have you heard of it?

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:23.810
I go there all the time!

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:26.020
Their black soybean cookies are exquisite!

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:30.020
Here. Try some freshly baked ones.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:38.740
And some of the tea you just gave me...
packaged and sold by yours truly.

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:41.410
What?

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:18.510
I can't believe you're selling products to the Mujina store...

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:24.720
I'm impressed, irritating as it is to admit.

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:26.310
Why, thank you.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:30.350
What about Hakumei? Where's she working?

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:35.480
She's sharpening and polishing knives for a gourmet restaurant.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:39.280
I must say I'm somewhat relieved.

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:45.870
I just wasn't sure if your gluttonous appetites were being satisfied by your own labors.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:49.120
Oww...

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:58.460
What are you making now?

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:02.260
Honey waffles. I'm trying out new items to sell.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:05.140
Honey... on waffles?

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:07.680
That sounds downright <i>seductive</i>!

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.020
Don't try to worm your way into "taste testing."

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:11.310
Let me help!

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:12.140
Huh?

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:17.110
At this rate I'll be no match for you!

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:20.030
What does that even mean?

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:23.700
Come on, please! I won't weigh you down!

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:30.950
Okay, whip the egg and honey together.

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:32.160
Understood!

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.500
Use a low flame to make a bain-marie.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:38.920
A bain-what, now?

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.300
What? I have to explain <i>that</i>?

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:48.010
Fill that pot over there with water, and over a low flame, submerge it in water with a bowl to heat it.

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:49.810
Did you get all that?

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:51.850
I definitely got most of it.

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:55.140
Now then! How do we get this stove going?

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:56.940
I'm concerned.

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:07.910
Maybe I should go lighter on the rum...

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:09.950
Or maybe even change it to kirsch.

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:17.670
Konju? What's that noise I h—

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:18.670
Huh?!

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.630
The stove's way too hot!

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:24.090
But I put the flame at the very bottom.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:27.090
That's not what low flame means! Just put it out!

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:37.400
I never would've imagined that you didn't know what a low flame is.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:40.900
I'm sorry, okay? I'm not very good with fire.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:45.030
Well, how are you at wrapping?

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:51.240
Wow! Nicely done!

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:55.910
Work like this is meant for a maiden like me!

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:56.750
All right, then.

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:00.750
I'll leave these to you.

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:02.130
What's this?

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:05.880
Dried sweet potato and dried persimmon, pickled radishes.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:08.430
Ten cans each of peach and pear jam.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:11.600
Wheat bread, jasmine tea, pickled ginger.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:13.560
And plenty of other stuff!

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:15.520
Ah. I see.

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:21.560
Do you usually do this by yourself?

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:27.150
I get Hakumei to help me.
I'm usually just doing the cooking and shopping.

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:30.780
But Hakumei has her own job, doesn't she?

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:33.080
She can usually do her work here at home.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:35.540
And she doesn't get much work in the first place.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:36.500
I see...

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:40.670
Well, if a handyman has little to do,

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:44.840
it must mean she did a good job the first time.

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:52.470
I see, I see.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:54.560
What?

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:59.100
You must be happy I came over today.

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:02.730
Yeah, I guess.

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:05.940
You get lonely pretty easily, I see.

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:07.320
Huh?

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:10.660
Stop talking nonsense. Come on, here's the last one.

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:11.860
Okay, okay.

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:24.500
Mikochi, what's this?

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:29.760
Test products. For a line of soaps.

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:30.840
Seriously?

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:36.760
How utterly devoid of beauty and style.
They're not even scented.

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:39.100
I-It doesn't matter, does it?

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.690
It most certainly does!

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:42.770
A maiden's scent is the scent of her soap!

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:45.560
A maiden's beauty is the beauty of her soap!

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:47.980
Sorry. I don't really understand.

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:52.030
Fetch some potpourri and oils.
And make some more of that tea.

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:54.120
Just what are you going to do?

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:58.620
This time, we're dealing in <i>my</i> specialty!

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:02.580
First, we grate up the soap.

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:05.130
It doesn't have to be grated all that finely.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:06.790
Mikochi, what about the oils?

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:11.380
Um, I have rose, chamomile,
mandarin, and mint...

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:14.510
That's sufficient. Brew the tea strong.

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:16.260
O-On it.

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:20.560
Now we crumble up the potpourri and lightly grind it up with this mortar.

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:24.770
Add a few drops of oil to the ground-up soap and potpourri,

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:26.860
and then just a touch of honey.

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:30.740
Stir it throughly while slowly adding the tea.

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:36.660
Pack the paste into a soapberry rind about the size of your palm.

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:40.410
And for the final touch...

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:49.000
Press a key and a brooch into the soap to add a design. And we're done!

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.420
Amazing! It looks completely different!

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:52.630
What did I tell you?

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:55.590
My grandmother taught me the whole process.

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:00.770
But she didn't teach you to cook?

00:09:06.810 --> 00:09:10.820
It smells so good! I'd be proud to have these up for sale!

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:16.280
It suds up pretty well. It would have been better if you had rosemary, though.

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:19.620
Well? Have I impressed you?

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:23.910
Konju, look! This is the one I put the chamomile oil in!

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:27.250
Ah, right, right. If you could just wash away the bubbles...

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:30.630
The mint soap feels so nice, too!

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:34.800
My eyes! Stop it, Mikochi! It'll get in my eyes!

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:42.680
Thanks for everything today, Konju.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:44.350
Likewise.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:48.060
I got to see something quite unusual, so I enjoyed myself.

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:51.820
I'll come back so I can see you
lose yourself in excitement again.

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:54.070
Please forget that happened.

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:58.360
I'll learn what low flame is by the time I come back!

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:15.970
Tidying up can wait 'til tomorrow, right?

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:24.220
Oh? So that's where this soap came from?

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:26.890
It certainly smells good.

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:28.480
Doesn't it?

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:33.320
What's this?

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:40.240
Oh? Where's my key?

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:48.500
Oh, here we go.

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:50.880
Rosemary.

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:54.880
Mikochi! I found rosemary!

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:58.970
Thanks! The soap will be even better now!

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:02.140
Thanks to Konju's advice, huh?

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:04.720
Speaking of Konju,

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:08.350
I wonder how she got into her house yesterday,
since she didn't have the key.

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:30.580
You know, I don't mind putting neighbors up for the night.

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:35.840
But I'm not so sure about you claiming the bed for yourself.

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:38.300
This bed's hard as a rock...

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:43.720
And I'm not sure about you taking all of your clothes
off in my room without a bit of hesitation, either.

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:47.010
I just can't sleep with my clothes on.

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:49.350
Hey, get up!

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:52.770
Hup!

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:56.860
Rocky mountain herbs sure smell nice.

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:57.900
Yep.

00:11:57.900 --> 00:12:00.030
We got a good haul of basil, too.

00:12:00.610 --> 00:12:04.700
For bread, or pizza, or pasta sauce, or piccata!

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:07.160
Keep your mind on the climb, or you'll fall.

00:12:07.530 --> 00:12:11.870
Anyway, I'd really like to get away from here as soon as possible.

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:19.210
This whole area is part of Oroshi's territory.

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:20.800
Oroshi?

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:23.220
They say he's a fearsome hunter.

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:26.510
Would he hunt <i>us</i>?

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:28.260
I can't really say...

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:34.480
Anyhow, if you hear his call, just dump all your dried meat and make a run for it.

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:36.860
Wh-What kind of call does he make?

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:41.530
Oh yeah. It's kinda like that.

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:57.250
Mikochi!

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:14.940
Hey, you okay?!

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:16.350
Mikochi!

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:21.650
Ow...

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:23.690
Don't move yet!

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:25.610
Where does it hurt?

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:28.490
My leg. My leg hurts.

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:30.160
Any nausea? Headache?

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:32.870
No, neither.

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:39.420
Once I've done first aid, I'm gonna get you out of here. All right?

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:40.750
Yeah.

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:51.140
Ow...

00:13:51.140 --> 00:13:52.470
Bear with it.

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:55.770
I didn't know there was a cave like this around here.

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:59.730
I stayed the night here once.

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:03.320
The feeling of tension and freedom from not having walls around you is great.

00:14:03.940 --> 00:14:08.740
It's not so great right now, though.
I'm not keen on staying here too long.

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:10.870
I'm sorry.

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:11.910
Don't worry about it.

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:18.170
It's pretty spacious in here.

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:22.170
Yeah. We'll camp out here today.

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:26.260
Does it hurt?

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:30.010
Yeah. I don't think I can walk for now.

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:38.440
All right. I'll go grab the stuff we left behind.

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:42.230
Are you going be okay on your own, Hakumei?

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:45.730
I oughta be asking you that question.

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:50.780
Don't worry, I'll be right back.

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:18.810
Now, I'll gather a few wild vegetables.
I'll also need some dry wood, and maybe some...

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:20.940
Whoops.

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:24.820
Maybe I've got too much.

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:40.250
Oroshi.

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:04.440
What?

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:06.770
What do you want?

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:10.320
If you eat me, will that be enough for you?

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:18.240
The dried meat?

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:23.830
You... You can have it. Go on, take it.

00:16:48.770 --> 00:16:50.280
Hakumei!

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:51.530
Welcome back...

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:58.990
Wh-What happened, Hakumei?

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:03.040
Mikochi... That was kinda scary.

00:17:03.910 --> 00:17:06.540
I'm sorry. All the meat got taken.

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:09.540
Um, that's okay.

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:13.970
Well, what happened?

00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:17.300
It was Oroshi.

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:18.850
I met him again.

00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:21.390
What? Were you okay?

00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:23.980
I gave him the meat, and he flew away.

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:29.650
Maybe that means that he's nice?

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:31.820
Let's hope so.

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:37.820
Yeah, that'll do.

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:39.740
It's a bit spicy.

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:43.660
I haven't had your cooking in ages.

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:54.300
It's delicious! This is the summer savory I'm tasting, right? It's really warming me up.

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:57.090
Good thing we brought roasted beans.

00:17:58.010 --> 00:18:01.850
We've got plenty of herbs,
and I found some wild vegetables,

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:04.680
so we should be able to hole up here for a while.

00:18:09.060 --> 00:18:10.480
Hakumei...

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:12.980
Are you scared?

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:19.950
The pain in my leg is fading.
I'll probably be able to walk tomorrow.

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:22.370
No, it's more like...

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:29.040
If Oroshi had attacked, I wouldn't have wanted to run off and leave you behind.

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:34.130
Oh... I see.

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:38.840
Have a rest once you're done eating. I'll clean up here.

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:49.520
Hey, Hakumei.

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:53.690
When did you learn to make that dish?

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:56.780
Oh, that? I learned it back during my vagabond days.

00:18:57.900 --> 00:19:02.530
It was back when I passed through that market town down south.

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:06.160
I lost everything. All my money and provisions.

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:08.370
What? Why?

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:10.420
You're not gonna get to sleep, are you?

00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:13.750
A pair of thieves stole it all.

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:20.510
A merchant told me he would let me eat some interesting food, free of charge.

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:28.480
And then his buddy got me while I was stuffing my face.

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:32.900
I walked for half a day before I realized it.

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:36.440
Everything in my bag had been replaced with rocks.

00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:43.910
Right when I was on the verge of death,
I was saved by a wolf and her caravan.

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:48.950
And what they gave me to eat was that bean soup.

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:55.040
Well, I guess they gave me all sorts of things.
Tasty food, and not-so-tasty food too.

00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:57.090
That sounds wonderful.

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:02.300
Fermented foods in particular always had a strong local flavor.

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:03.680
Sometimes they'd be rotten.

00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:06.970
I wonder if I could make them. For example...

00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:08.850
What kind of—

00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:21.240
Hakumei, I'm coming with you.

00:20:23.610 --> 00:20:24.990
Mikochi...

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:30.250
If things go bad, you run back in here.

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:31.830
I will.

00:20:56.690 --> 00:21:00.190
Could that... possibly be...

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:02.990
For us?

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:20.960
Off he goes.

00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:25.380
Maybe it's in return for the dried meat?

00:21:28.050 --> 00:21:30.430
Now I just feel drained.

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:32.720
What are we going to do with all this?

00:21:33.180 --> 00:21:36.980
Do you think you could rustle up a midnight snack?

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:40.480
I thought you might say that. Leave it to me.

00:21:46.610 --> 00:21:50.700
Just the bean soup really wasn't enough.

00:21:50.700 --> 00:21:52.870
It was tasty, though.

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:56.500
Tell me another one of your stories while I'm cooking.

00:21:56.920 --> 00:21:58.830
Well then, I'll give you the best I've got.

00:21:58.830 --> 00:22:02.250
It's about when I met a herd of cows. Want to hear it?

00:22:02.250 --> 00:22:05.670
I've never seen a cow before!

00:22:27.400 --> 00:22:35.500
When the breeze is pleasant, let's eat outside

00:22:35.500 --> 00:22:43.300
The olives are fragrant this time of year

00:22:43.300 --> 00:22:47.300
And in the plum-colored sky,

00:22:47.300 --> 00:22:51.260
the stars twinkle and shine

00:22:51.260 --> 00:22:55.810
After we take in an easy breath,

00:22:55.810 --> 00:23:00.190
the banquet will begin!

00:23:00.190 --> 00:23:03.820
A freshly-made smoked cheese quiche,

00:23:03.820 --> 00:23:07.530
sockeye salmon wrapped in magnolia leaves

00:23:07.530 --> 00:23:11.450
Look, the whole world is rejoicing

00:23:11.450 --> 00:23:16.290
It's itching to dance with us

00:23:16.290 --> 00:23:20.250
And what drink might fit a night like this?

00:23:20.250 --> 00:23:24.210
How about something botanical with pepper in it?

00:23:24.210 --> 00:23:29.510
We could even catch the moon with our tiny hands

00:23:29.510 --> 00:23:33.050
At least, that's how we're feeling
